<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Godavaya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Godavaya is an archaeological site on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, near the mouth of the Walawe river in Hambantota District. An ancient harbour there is recorded in an early inscription granting its customs dues to a Buddhist monastery, and a shipwreck found offshore, dated to between the 2nd century BCE and the 1st century CE, is among the oldest known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. It shows the southern kingdom of Ruhuna's part in early maritime trade.</p></div>
